  "result": "Fixed: `quote a:12.5:2` now prints **27.06**.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py:9` padded the decimal part on the wrong side. It used `frac.rjust(2, \"0\")`, which turns `\"5\"` into `\"05\"`, so `\"12.5\"` became 1205 cents (12.05) instead of 1250. Two of those come to 24.10, and with 8.25% tax that's 26.09. Prices with two decimals were unaffected, which is why the existing tests passed.\n\n**Fix:** I changed it to `frac.ljust(2, \"0\")`, so `\"5\"` becomes `\"50\"`. I also added a regression test, `MoneyTests.test_to_cents_pads_single_decimal`, in `tests/test_pricing.py`. All 7 tests pass.\n\nThere's a separate problem in the same function that I didn't touch: it gets negative amounts wrong. `to_cents(\"-1.50\")` returns -50 instead of -150, because the fraction is added to a negative whole number. The CLI doesn't hit this with normal prices, but tell me if you want it fixed too.",
